---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { levels } from '../../data/psl';
---

<Legal
  title="Responsible Scaling Policy"
  description="How Pugalarity Labs ties deployment decisions to capability thresholds, from reaching the couch to operating a doorknob."
  lead="Our commitment to scaling capabilities only as fast as we can scale safeguards."
>
  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Purpose</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      As our models grow more capable, so do the risks they pose. This policy defines capability
      thresholds, the safeguards required at each, and the conditions under which we will pause
      development or deployment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Pug Safety Levels</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We assess every model against the following thresholds before training continues or
      deployment begins.
    </p>
    <table class="mt-5 w-full text-left text-base">
      <caption class="sr-only">Pug Safety Levels, with the capability threshold and required safeguards for each</caption>
      <thead class="border-rule border-b">
        <tr>
          <th scope="col" class="py-3 pr-3 font-medium">Level</th>
          <th scope="col" class="py-3 pr-3 font-medium">Capability threshold</th>
          <th scope="col" class="py-3 font-medium">Required safeguards</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-rule divide-y">
        {
          levels.map(([level, threshold, safeguards]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="whitespace-nowrap py-3 pr-3 align-top font-mono font-medium">{level}</th>
              <td class="py-3 pr-3 align-top">{threshold}</td>
              <td class="text-muted py-3 align-top">{safeguards}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Deployment decisions</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Snort-1 is currently assessed at PSL-2 and is deployed in private preview. If a model
      reaches PSL-3, deployment halts until pantry gates are installed and independently
      verified. We will not train a model to PSL-4.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Incident reporting</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Incidents involving the pantry are reported internally within 24 hours, or upon discovery of
      the wrapper, whichever comes first.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Governance</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      This policy is overseen by the Board of Directors, which has final authority over scaling
      decisions. The Board has not been consulted and has not objected.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
